From: yah <yah@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:50:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 41/73] 0040-loom-amdgpu-b16-store-takes-low-half-def

Loom: a 16-bit VGPR store writes bits 0..15 of its data register only, so a payload defined by a low-half write
(v_cvt_f16_f32 to .l and friends) is stored as it is. The store lowering cleared the upper half first with
v_bfe_u32 x, 0, 16 for every such store. gen_gdn_ss: 168 v_bfe_u32 removed (solver loop 915 -> 849 VALU per
chunk, row loop 1017 -> 993), bit-identical.

(cherry picked from commit 26ef9d3bf076d65852163100cdc80219aad048d3)
---
 loom/src/loom/target/arch/amdgpu/lower/memory_emit.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amdgpu/lower/memory_emit.c b/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amdgpu/lower/memory_emit.c
index 4503b29ca9..098159b583 100644
--- a/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amdgpu/lower/memory_emit.c
+++ b/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amdgpu/lower/memory_emit.c
@@ -124,10 +124,9 @@ static iree_status_t loom_amdgpu_ensure_memory_store_payload_vgpr(
   const bool is_vgpr = loom_amdgpu_low_type_is_register_class(
       context, low_type, LOOM_AMDGPU_REG_CLASS_ID_VGPR);
   if (is_vgpr) {
-    if (access->payload_register_count == 1 && access->packet_byte_count == 2) {
-      return loom_amdgpu_materialize_full_low_vgpr_b32(
-          context, source_op, low_value, out_low_value);
-    }
+    // A 16-bit store writes bits 0..15 of its data register only: a value
+    // defined by a low-half write stores as it is, without clearing the
+    // upper half first.
     return iree_ok_status();
   }
   const bool is_sgpr = loom_amdgpu_low_type_is_register_class(
